# ── Provider ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pick one provider and uncomment its block.  Everything else stays the same;
# all 11 harnesses derive their endpoint+key+model from these three vars:
#
#   PROVIDER_BASE_URL       OpenAI-compatible URL ending in /v1 (most harnesses)
#   PROVIDER_API_KEY        bearer token the provider expects
#   MODEL_NAME              model id in the provider's own format
#
# Anthropic-compatible harnesses (Claude Code, Droid) additionally need:
#   PROVIDER_ANTHROPIC_URL  base URL exposing /v1/messages (typically the same
#                           host without the /v1 suffix)
#
# Most non-NIM providers do not implement Anthropic's /v1/messages surface;
# leave PROVIDER_ANTHROPIC_URL pointing at the same host anyway (the SDK will
# 404 cleanly), and use one of the 11 OpenAI-compat harnesses instead.
#
# Quick verification before relying on a provider:
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $PROVIDER_API_KEY" $PROVIDER_BASE_URL/models
# Make sure the model you picked supports tool/function calling.

# --- NVIDIA NIM (self-hosted) -------------------------------------------------
PROVIDER_BASE_URL=http://nim.example.com:8000/v1
PROVIDER_ANTHROPIC_URL=http://nim.example.com:8000
PROVIDER_API_KEY=nvapi-replace-me
MODEL_NAME=deepseek-ai/deepseek-coder-v2-instruct

# --- OpenRouter (hosted, ~300 models) -----------------------------------------
# PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# PROVIDER_ANTHROPIC_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
# PROVIDER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# MODEL_NAME=anthropic/claude-3.5-sonnet

# --- build.nvidia.com (NIM hosted by NVIDIA, free tier) -----------------------
# PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
# PROVIDER_ANTHROPIC_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com
# PROVIDER_API_KEY=nvapi-...
# MODEL_NAME=meta/llama-3.1-405b-instruct

# --- Anthropic direct (real Claude — most expensive, best at tool calling) ---
# PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1
# PROVIDER_ANTHROPIC_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# PROVIDER_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# MODEL_NAME=claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022

# --- OpenAI direct ------------------------------------------------------------
# PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# PROVIDER_ANTHROPIC_URL=https://api.openai.com
# PROVIDER_API_KEY=sk-...
# MODEL_NAME=gpt-4o

# --- Groq (fast Llama/Mixtral, OpenAI-compat) ---------------------------------
# PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# PROVIDER_ANTHROPIC_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai
# PROVIDER_API_KEY=gsk_...
# MODEL_NAME=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# --- Together.ai --------------------------------------------------------------
# PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://api.together.xyz/v1
# PROVIDER_ANTHROPIC_URL=https://api.together.xyz
# PROVIDER_API_KEY=...
# MODEL_NAME=deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3

# --- DeepSeek direct ----------------------------------------------------------
# PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
# PROVIDER_ANTHROPIC_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic
# PROVIDER_API_KEY=sk-...
# MODEL_NAME=deepseek-chat

# --- Local Ollama (no GPU? use small models like qwen2.5-coder:7b) ------------
# PROVIDER_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# PROVIDER_ANTHROPIC_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434
# PROVIDER_API_KEY=ollama
# MODEL_NAME=qwen2.5-coder:7b

# ── Free-model catalog / fallback (OpenRouter only) ───────────────────────────
# The auth service serves a self-updating /v1/models catalog to the harness
# pickers and can inject a `models` fallback array on every request.  Two knobs:
#
#   FREE_FALLBACK=1        On a rate-limit/error, OpenRouter rolls the request
#                          over to the next free model (resilient).  The switch
#                          is transparent: the reply leads with a one-line
#                          "↳ <requested> unavailable → answered by <served>"
#                          notice, the response reports the model that actually
#                          answered, and the proxy logs every switch.  Set 0 to
#                          always use exactly the model you selected (you'll get
#                          a clear error instead of any substitution).
#   FREE_REQUIRE_TOOLS=1   Catalog lists only tool-calling models (needed for
#                          agentic work).  Set 0 to list *every* free model in
#                          the pickers (chat-only models included).
#
# Defaults preserve the resilient/tool-only behaviour.  For a comparison lab
# where you hand-pick each model, set both to 0:
# FREE_FALLBACK=0
# FREE_REQUIRE_TOOLS=0

# ── OpenCode Go for Claude Code (optional) ────────────────────────────────────
# A second provider next to OpenRouter, for Claude Code only.  With the key set,
# Claude Code's /model picker lists every OpenCode Go model as
# `opencode-go/<id>` after the free OpenRouter ones (or type
# `/model opencode-go/kimi-k3`).  Those requests are billed to the Go
# subscription; every other model stays on OpenRouter.  It is the key `/connect`
# stores in the opencode harness.  Blank = no Go models and no route.
#
# Only the containers in OPENCODE_GO_CLIENTS may spend it, so the sweep and the
# other harnesses cannot.  Some Go models (DeepSeek V4) answer 403 RegionError
# until you opt in to their China hosting on your Go workspace page.
# OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY=
# OPENCODE_GO_CLIENTS=harness-claude

# The Claude harness's own default model.  Any id its /model picker accepts,
# e.g. a Go model.  It wins over a model saved with /model, so each launch
# starts here; /model still switches for the session.  It fills every model
# slot (main session, subagents, and the Opus and Haiku slots that session
# titles, WebFetch summaries and Explore subagents use), so a session never
# waits on a free OpenRouter model.  Blank = MODEL_NAME, like every other
# harness.
# Claude Code assumes a 200k context window for a model it doesn't recognize,
# and compacts at that size. Append [1m] to a 1M-context model to fix that; it
# strips the suffix before the request goes out.
# CLAUDE_MODEL=opencode-go/muse-spark-1.3-contributor[1m]

# ── Domain / cookies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All harness subdomains live under this base. Set a *.lab.example.com DNS A
# record pointing at this VPS. Cookies are scoped to the leading dot so a single
# JWT cookie issued at e.g. aider.lab.example.com stays restricted to that host.
HARNESS_BASE_DOMAIN=lab.example.com

# ── Auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Long random string used to sign per-harness JWTs. Rotate by regenerating
# tokens (scripts/generate-tokens.py) — the secret change invalidates all
# existing tokens immediately.
JWT_SECRET=replace-me-with-a-long-random-string

# ── Session longevity ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The browser cookie holds a SESSION token minted at login, not the TOKEN_*
# below: logging in on any subdomain starts a fresh SESSION_TTL_DAYS window,
# and the auth service re-mints (slides) the cookie once less than
# SESSION_REFRESH_DAYS of that window remain — so a session in regular use
# never lapses. Both are days.
SESSION_TTL_DAYS=360
SESSION_REFRESH_DAYS=30

# all     → the session covers EVERY subdomain under HARNESS_BASE_DOMAIN
#           (all harnesses, every <harness>-<slug> session, and files) — one
#           login for the whole lab. This is the single-operator default.
# harness → the session stays pinned to the harness it was minted on, so a
#           login on claude.<domain> does not unlock files.<domain>.
SESSION_SCOPE=all

# Idle timeout (minutes) before the auth service stops a harness container
# (measured from the last moment a browser tab held a connection or the
# harness called a model through this proxy, so an open tab or a working agent
# keeps it awake). Set to 0 to disable auto-stop. One value covers every
# harness; add "<harness>=<minutes>" to override one, e.g. "360,opencode=120"
# to give up a heavier harness sooner. 30 is a sane default now
# that waking resumes the conversation rather than starting blank: an idle
# harness can hold ~1GB, and the cost of getting it back is one cold start
# (seconds for most, ~a minute for claude, which re-registers its MCP servers
# first). But a stop restarts every session in the container, and slug
# sessions (<harness>-<slug>) come back blank, so raise it (720 = 12 hours) if
# you leave those unattended. A phone drops its tab connection when locked.
IDLE_TIMEOUT_MIN=30

# Seconds the auth service waits for a cold-starting harness to start
# listening before giving up with a 504. Must cover the SLOWEST harness boot:
# claude's entrypoint registers ~26 MCP servers before it execs ttyd, which
# can take over a minute.
COLD_START_TIMEOUT_S=120

# Harness types the idle sweep must NEVER stop (comma-separated, e.g.
# "claude,opencode"). Stopping a container kills its tmux server and every CLI
# session running inside it. Empty by default, which is usually right: a stop
# returns all of the harness's RAM, and the next visit starts it again (~40s
# for claude). Exempt one whose container hosts something a stop would take
# down, or whose cold start you can't tolerate; its RAM then comes back only
# through SESSION_IDLE_HOURS below. Note that a stopped container is what
# `docker container prune` deletes — the auth service rebuilds one from its
# saved spec (_recreate_container), since it can start a container but not
# create one.
IDLE_EXEMPT=

# Max dynamic instances (claude-<slug>, aider-<slug>, …) allowed to run in
# parallel per harness type.  The always-on base harness is not counted.
# Set to 0 for unlimited.  A request for a (cap+1)th distinct slug is rejected.
MAX_INSTANCES_PER_HARNESS=5

# Days of inactivity before an unpinned dynamic session (<harness>-<slug>) is
# torn down by the retention sweep. Pin a session (POST /pin) to exempt it.
RETENTION_DAYS=7

# Hours one session may sit with no browser tab connected before the idle
# sweep closes it: a dynamic session (<harness>-<slug>) -- its CLI process
# (~1GB for opencode) and its ttyd; and on an IDLE_EXEMPT harness, whose
# container never stops, the `main` session's CLI too (never its ttyd, which is
# that container's PID 1). The container and every other session keep running.
# Reconnecting starts the session again: `main` resumes its conversation, a
# slug comes back fresh (its conversation stays in history/). Pinned sessions
# are kept. 0 disables. One value covers every harness; add "<harness>=<hours>"
# to override one, e.g. "24,opencode=3" to get opencode's RAM back sooner.
SESSION_IDLE_HOURS=24

# ── Per-harness JWTs (regenerate with scripts/generate-tokens.py) ─────────────
TOKEN_CLAUDE=
TOKEN_AIDER=
TOKEN_OPENCODE=
TOKEN_CRUSH=
TOKEN_GPTME=
TOKEN_GOOSE=
TOKEN_PLANDEX=
TOKEN_QWENCODE=
TOKEN_CODEX=
TOKEN_PI=
TOKEN_DROID=
# Not a CLI harness — the always-on file-manager web UI at files.<domain>.
TOKEN_FILES=

# ─── Folio MCP server (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Connects the harnesses to an external Folio MCP instance. Leave blank to
# disable. Each harness entrypoint registers it in its native MCP config format.
FOLIO_MCP_URL=https://folio.your-domain.tld/mcp
FOLIO_MCP_TOKEN=sk-folio-...

# ─── Pipeline MCP server (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# github.com/azzindani/Pipeline. Registered by the claude harness only.
#
# PIPELINE_MCP_IMAGE — a locally built Pipeline image (`docker compose build` in
# the Pipeline repo → pipeline:latest). Its binary is baked into harness-claude
# at build time and runs over stdio on /workspace: writes, runs, memory, plans.
# Rebuild harness-claude after rebuilding Pipeline. Blank → no local binary.
PIPELINE_MCP_IMAGE=
# PIPELINE_PROJECT — directory Pipeline roots itself at (its pipeline.yaml).
# Blank → the session's cwd (/workspace). /workspace holds several projects, so
# point it at the one being built, e.g. /workspace/my-app.
PIPELINE_PROJECT=
#
# Remote fallback, used only when the image carries no binary. The endpoint
# runs PIPELINE_REMOTE_MODE=read_only on its own /work, so it cannot write or
# run anything and never sees /workspace. Bearer = that deployment's
# PIPELINE_TOKEN. Leave blank to disable.
PIPELINE_MCP_URL=https://pipeline.your-domain.tld/mcp
PIPELINE_MCP_TOKEN=sk-pipeline-...

# ─── Web search/fetch MCP (DuckDuckGo, free, no API key) ────────────────────
# Always-on sidecar (service web-mcp) on harnesses_net. Every harness registers
# this URL in its native MCP config. No token. Leave blank to disable.
WEB_MCP_URL=http://web-mcp:7070/mcp
# DDG_SAFE_SEARCH=MODERATE   # STRICT | MODERATE | OFF

# ─── MCP_* self-hosted tool servers (optional, 7 repos) ─────────────────────
# github.com/azzindani/MCP_{Math,Web_Browser,File_System,Machine_Learning,
# Data_Analyst,Microsoft_Office,Documents} — each deployed standalone,
# bearer-token auth, registered the same env-var-gated way as Folio/web above.
# Leave a pair blank to disable that repo entirely. Math/Browser/File_System
# expose one endpoint each; the rest mount several sub-servers with no single
# unified endpoint, so their var is the BASE url (no /mcp suffix) and each
# harness entrypoint registers every sub-server under it individually.
# Every host below is a placeholder — substitute your own.
MATH_MCP_URL=https://math.your-domain.tld/mcp
MATH_MCP_TOKEN=sk-math-...

# Browser automation (fetch/extract/search) — distinct from the bundled
# DuckDuckGo `web` sidecar above.
BROWSER_MCP_URL=https://browser.your-domain.tld/mcp
BROWSER_MCP_TOKEN=sk-browser-...

FS_MCP_URL=https://fs.your-domain.tld/mcp
FS_MCP_TOKEN=sk-fs-...

# 3 sub-servers: basic, medium, advanced.
ML_MCP_BASE_URL=https://ml.your-domain.tld
ML_MCP_TOKEN=sk-ml-...

# 7 sub-servers: basic, medium, statistics, transform, visual, workspace, ingest.
DATA_MCP_BASE_URL=https://data.your-domain.tld
DATA_MCP_TOKEN=sk-data-...

# 11 sub-servers: docx-{basic,tables,layout,new}, xlsx-{basic,formulas,charts,new},
# pptx-{basic,design,new}.
OFFICE_MCP_BASE_URL=https://office.your-domain.tld
OFFICE_MCP_TOKEN=sk-office-...

# 2 sub-servers: read, edit.
DOCS_MCP_BASE_URL=https://docs.your-domain.tld
DOCS_MCP_TOKEN=sk-docs-...

# Servers to leave out of a harness, comma-separated. Matches either a whole
# registered entry name (`browser`, `folio`, `office-xlsx-new`) or a repo
# prefix, so `office` removes all 11 of its mounts at once. The budget here is
# the tool namespace, not RAM: every extra tool costs selection accuracy and
# schema tokens in a small context, so hide what a given harness will not use.
# Honored by the opencode and claude harnesses, which therefore see the same
# set; the other harnesses still register everything.
#MCP_DISABLED=browser,filesystem,office-xlsx-basic

# harness-sweep only. Its compose entry sets MCP_DISABLED from this var
# instead of the one above, so scoping your day-to-day harness never blinds
# the sweep — the hidden servers are exactly the repos it is meant to test.
# Leave unset.
#SWEEP_MCP_DISABLED=

# opencode harness only. A provider-qualified id opencode already knows
# (`opencode models`), used with that provider's own endpoint and credentials
# instead of the shared OpenRouter route. Unset = shared route, as before.
#OPENCODE_MODEL=opencode/muse-spark-1.2-contributor-free

# harness-sweep only, same idea as OPENCODE_MODEL: the sweep's own opencode
# runs with an empty opencode.db and therefore no credentials, so it can only
# reach the anonymous free tier and never a paid subscription.
#SWEEP_MODEL=
